ntdll: Skip the server on would-block receives from nonblocking sockets.

DOOM 2016's DTLS thread polls a nonblocking UDP socket with recvfrom() in a
loop; every empty poll cost two server requests (recv_socket and
set_async_direct_result), 95 % of all requests and a quarter of a core in
wineserver. The server now grants a poll_fastpath to a plain nonblocking
receive on a socket with a single handle, no event or message select, no
queued reads and no pending AcceptEx; later receives on that handle that
poll() finds nothing for fail with STATUS_DEVICE_NOT_READY in ntdll. Every
256th answer goes back to the server, and the grant is dropped on close,
duplicate and every socket ioctl the server handles. IOCTL_AFD_EVENT_SELECT
now drops a reported READ event whose data is already gone.

Switch: WINE_SOCKET_POLL_FASTPATH=0 disables it.

PR: https://github.com/GameNative/proton-wine/pull/119

